{"book":"PSA","chapter":28,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9],"records":[{"id":"PSA.28.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"לְדָוִ֡דאֵ֘לֶ֤יךָ יְהוָ֨ה׀אֶקְרָ֗א צוּרִי֮ אַֽל־תֶּחֱרַ֪שׁ מִ֫מֶּ֥נִּי פֶּן־תֶּֽחֱשֶׁ֥ה מִמֶּ֑נִּי וְ֝נִמְשַׁ֗לְתִּי עִם־י֥וֹרְדֵי בֽוֹר׃","gloss":"Of David. To you, YHWH, I call; my rock, do not be deaf to me, lest you be silent to me and I become like those going down [to the] pit.","pieces":[[1,"Of David. I call to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}, {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}; my rock, do not refuse to hear me. For if {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} say nothing to me, I will be like those who sink into the pit.",null]],"L":{"1":"Of David. To {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}, {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, I call; my rock, do not be deaf to me, lest, if {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} are silent to me, I become like those who go down [to the] pit."},"R":{"1":"By David. {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, I am calling to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}. You are my rock. Please listen to me! If {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} do not answer me, I will soon be among the dead in the grave."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"punctuation","tokens":["o190280010011","o190280010012"],"choice":"The title shares verse 1","alternatives":[],"reason":"This psalm's title is short and the Hebrew counts it together with the first line as verse 1, so here the verse numbers are the same as in Bibles that print the title without a number.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190280010051"],"choice":"my rock: my safe place","alternatives":[],"reason":"A rock is a place of refuge and strength; God is called the psalmist's rock (18:3; 31:4).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280010151"],"choice":"the pit: the grave, the world of the dead","alternatives":[],"reason":"The pit (bor) is the grave and the place of the dead (30:4; 88:5).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190280010071","o190280010101"],"choice":"be deaf, be silent: give no answer","alternatives":[],"reason":"A God who does not answer seems deaf and silent; to the psalmist that would be death.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190280010141","o190280010151"],"choice":"I will soon be among the dead in the grave","alternatives":["I become like those who go down to the pit"],"reason":"Readable says what the pit is (m2).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":"My rock, do not be silent","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.28.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"שְׁמַ֤ע ק֣וֹל תַּ֭חֲנוּנַי בְּשַׁוְּעִ֣י אֵלֶ֑יךָ בְּנָשְׂאִ֥י יָ֝דַ֗י אֶל־דְּבִ֥יר קָדְשֶֽׁךָ׃","gloss":"Hear [the] sound of my pleas when I cry to you for help, when I lift up my hands toward [the] inner room of your holiness.","pieces":[[2,"Listen to my voice as I beg for mercy and cry to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} for help, as I raise my hands toward the innermost room of {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} holy house.",null]],"L":{"2":"Hear the sound of my pleadings when I cry to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} for help, when I lift my hands toward the inner room of {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} holy place."},"R":{"2":"Listen to me as I beg {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} to help me. I am lifting my hands in prayer toward the holiest room in {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} temple."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o190280020091"],"choice":"the inner room: the most holy place","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (devir) is the innermost room of the sanctuary, where the ark stood (1 Kings 6:16, 19).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o190280020062","o190280020071"],"choice":"lift up my hands: the posture of prayer","alternatives":[],"reason":"People prayed standing with hands raised toward the sanctuary (134:2; 141:2).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280020031"],"choice":"pleadings: prayers for grace","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (tachanunim) is from the root of \"be gracious\": asking for mercy.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.28.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"אַל־תִּמְשְׁכֵ֣נִי עִם־רְשָׁעִים֮ וְעִם־פֹּ֪עֲלֵ֫י אָ֥וֶן דֹּבְרֵ֣י שָׁ֭לוֹם עִם־רֵֽעֵיהֶ֑ם וְ֝רָעָ֗ה בִּלְבָבָֽם׃","gloss":"Do not drag me away with wicked [people] and with workers of iniquity, speaking peace with their neighbors, and evil [is] in their heart.","pieces":[[3,"Do not haul me away along with the wicked and the evildoers, who wish their neighbors peace while they plan harm in their hearts.",null]],"L":{"3":"Do not drag me away with [the] wicked and with workers of iniquity, who speak peace with their neighbors while evil [is] in their heart."},"R":{"3":"Do not take me away with wicked people who do evil things. They say friendly words to their neighbors, but they are planning to hurt them."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190280030021"],"choice":"drag me away: to judgment and death","alternatives":[],"reason":"The psalmist asks not to be swept away in the judgment that falls on the wicked (26:9).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280030081","o190280030091"],"choice":"speak peace: greet as friends","alternatives":[],"reason":"To speak peace (shalom) is to greet someone and wish them well; these do it with harm in mind (compare 55:22).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280030061","o190280030071"],"choice":"workers of iniquity: people who do evil","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 5:6.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.28.4.s1","verses":[4],"source":"תֶּן־לָהֶ֣ם כְּפָעֳלָם֮ וּכְרֹ֪עַ מַֽעַלְלֵ֫יהֶ֥ם כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֣ה יְ֭דֵיהֶם תֵּ֣ן לָהֶ֑ם הָשֵׁ֖ב גְּמוּלָ֣ם לָהֶֽם׃","gloss":"Give to them according to their work and according to [the] evil of their deeds; according to [the] work of their hands give to them; return their recompense to them.","pieces":[[4,"Pay them back for what they do, for the evil of their actions; give them what their hands have earned; let what they deserve come back on them.",null]],"L":{"4":"Give to them according to their work and according to the evil of their deeds; according to the work of their hands give to them; bring back their recompense on them."},"R":{"4":"Punish them for the evil things they have done. Give them what they deserve for what they have done."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"theology","tokens":["o190280040011","o190280040101"],"choice":"repay them: a prayer for justice","alternatives":[],"reason":"The psalmist does not take revenge himself but asks God, the judge, to give the wicked what their deeds deserve (Deuteronomy 32:35; Psalm 94:1-2).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280040111"],"choice":"recompense: what they have earned","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (gemul) is a deed's due return, good or bad.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.28.5.s1","verses":[5],"source":"כִּ֤י לֹ֤א יָבִ֡ינוּ אֶל־פְּעֻלֹּ֣ת יְ֭הוָה וְאֶל־מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה יָדָ֑יו יֶ֝הֶרְסֵ֗ם וְלֹ֣א יִבְנֵֽם׃","gloss":"For they do not consider the deeds of YHWH and the work of his hands; he will tear them down and not build them up.","pieces":[[5,"Because they pay no attention to what {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} does or to what {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} hands have made, {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} will pull them down and not raise them up again.",null]],"L":{"5":"For they do not discern the deeds of {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} or the work of {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} hands; {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} will tear them down and not build them up."},"R":{"5":"They do not care about what {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} has done. So {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} will destroy them, and they will never be strong again."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280050031"],"choice":"consider: understand, pay attention to","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (bin) is to discern; they do not see God at work and so do not fear him.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190280050101","o190280050121"],"choice":"tear down, not build up: destroy for good","alternatives":[],"reason":"The pair is used of God's judgment and blessing (Jeremiah 1:10; 24:6).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.28.6.s1","verses":[6],"source":"בָּר֥וּךְ יְהוָ֑ה כִּי־שָׁ֝מַע ק֣וֹל תַּחֲנוּנָֽי׃","gloss":"Blessed [be] YHWH, for he has heard [the] sound of my pleas.","pieces":[[6,"Blessed is {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, because {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has listened to my voice as I pleaded.",null]],"L":{"6":"Blessed [be] {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, for {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has heard the sound of my pleadings."},"R":{"6":"Praise {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}! He has heard me when I begged {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} for help."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280060011"],"choice":"Blessed: praised","alternatives":[],"reason":"When people bless God (baruk), they praise and thank him; it is not the word 'ashre of 1:1.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o190280060041"],"choice":"he has heard: the prayer is answered","alternatives":[],"reason":"The psalm turns from plea to thanks: the plea of verse 2 has been heard. The same words (\"the sound of my pleadings\") answer it.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190280060011"],"choice":"Praise","alternatives":["Blessed be"],"reason":"Readable says what blessing God means (m1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.28.7.s1","verses":[7],"source":"יְהוָ֤ה׀עֻזִּ֥י וּמָגִנִּי֮ בּ֤וֹ בָטַ֥ח לִבִּ֗י וְֽנֶ֫עֱזָ֥רְתִּי וַיַּעֲלֹ֥ז לִבִּ֑י וּֽמִשִּׁירִ֥י אֲהוֹדֶֽנּוּ׃","gloss":"YHWH [is] my strength and my shield; in him my heart trusted, and I was helped; and my heart exulted, and with my song I will thank him.","pieces":[[7,"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} is my strength, the shield that protects me; my heart trusted in {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}, and help came to me. Now my heart is full of joy, and I will thank {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} in song.",null]],"L":{"7":"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} [is] my strength and my shield; in {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} my heart trusted, and I was helped; so my heart exults, and with my song I will give thanks to {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}."},"R":{"7":"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} makes me strong and protects me like a shield. I trusted {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}, and {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} helped me. My heart jumps for joy, and I will sing songs to thank {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190280070032"],"choice":"my shield: my protector","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 3:4.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o190280070051","o190280070072"],"choice":"trusted ... was helped: trust answered","alternatives":[],"reason":"The past forms tell what has happened: he trusted, and help came.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190280070072"],"choice":"he helped me","alternatives":["I was helped"],"reason":"Readable names who helped.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.28.8.s1","verses":[8],"source":"יְהוָ֥ה עֹֽז־לָ֑מוֹ וּמָ֘ע֤וֹז יְשׁוּע֖וֹת מְשִׁיח֣וֹ הֽוּא׃","gloss":"YHWH [is] strength to them, and [the] stronghold of saving acts of his anointed [is] he.","pieces":[[8,"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} is their strength; {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} is the fortress where {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} anointed one finds rescue.",null]],"L":{"8":"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} [is] strength for them, and a stronghold of salvation for {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} anointed [is] {{deity_pronoun:he|He}}."},"R":{"8":"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} makes {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} people strong. He is a safe place for the king {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has chosen, and {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} rescues him."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"text_variant","tokens":["o190280080031","o190280080032"],"choice":"for them: the Hebrew text","alternatives":["for his people (some Hebrew manuscripts and ancient translations)"],"reason":"The Hebrew reads \"strength to them\", meaning God's people. With one letter different, some Hebrew manuscripts and ancient translations read \"strength to his people\", as in 29:11. The sense is the same.","uncertain":true,"footnote":true},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280080061"],"choice":"his anointed: the king","alternatives":[],"reason":"The anointed one is the king God has chosen (2:2; 18:51). The prayer of a king becomes a prayer for the people (verse 9).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280080051"],"choice":"salvation: saving acts","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (yeshu'ot) is plural: one rescue after another.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190280080032"],"choice":"his people","alternatives":["them"],"reason":"Readable says who \"them\" is (m1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.28.9.s1","verses":[9],"source":"הוֹשִׁ֤יעָה׀אֶת־עַמֶּ֗ךָ וּבָרֵ֥ךְ אֶת־נַחֲלָתֶ֑ךָ וּֽרְעֵ֥ם וְ֝נַשְּׂאֵ֗ם עַד־הָעוֹלָֽם׃","gloss":"Save your people and bless your inheritance, and shepherd them and carry them until forever.","pieces":[[9,"Rescue {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} people, bless those who belong to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}; be a shepherd to them and carry them in {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} arms for all time.",null]],"L":{"9":"Save {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} people and bless {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} inheritance; shepherd them and carry them forever."},"R":{"9":"Save {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} people and bless them, because they belong to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}. Take care of them like a shepherd, and carry them always."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190280090061"],"choice":"your inheritance: the people who belong to God","alternatives":[],"reason":"Israel is God's inheritance (nachalah), his own possession (Deuteronomy 9:29).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190280090072","o190280090082"],"choice":"shepherd them and carry them","alternatives":[],"reason":"The LORD is the shepherd who carries his flock (Isaiah 40:11; Psalm 23:1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["B"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190280090082"],"choice":"in your arms","alternatives":[],"reason":"Balanced fills out the picture of the shepherd carrying lambs (m2).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190280090061"],"choice":"those who belong to you","alternatives":["your inheritance"],"reason":"Balanced and Readable say what the word means (m1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o190280010011","text":"לְ","after":"","lemma":"לְ","morph":"R","gloss":"of","strong":"3807a","transliteration":"lə","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o190280010012","text":"דָוִ֡ד","after":"","lemma":"דָּוִד","morph":"Np","gloss":"David","strong":"1732","transliteration":"ḏāwiḏ","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o190280010021","text":"אֵ֘לֶ֤י","after":"","lemma":"אֶל","morph":"R","gloss":"to","strong":"0413","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o190280010022","text":"ךָ","after":" ","lemma":"הוּא","morph":"Sp2ms","gloss":"you","strong":"3509b","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Suffix · pronoun · 2nd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o190280010031","text":"יְהוָ֨ה","after":"׀","lemma":"יהוה","morph":"Np","gloss":"O.Yahweh","strong":"3068","transliteration":"yəhwāh","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o190280010041","text":"אֶקְרָ֗א","after":" ","lemma":"קָרָא","morph":"Vqi1cs","gloss":"I.call.out","strong":"7121","transliteration":"ʾeqrāʾ","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Qal · imperfect (yiqtol) · 1st person common singular"},{"id":"o190280010051","text":"צוּרִ","after":"","lemma":"צוּר","morph":"Ncmsc","gloss":"my.rock","strong":"6697","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular construct (of ...)"},{"id":"o190280010052","text":"י֮","after":" ","lemma":"הוּא","morph":"Sp1cs","gloss":"my","strong":"2967a","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Suffix · pronoun · 1st person common singular"},{"id":"o190280010061","text":"אַֽל","after":"־","lemma":"אַל","morph":"Tn","gloss":"do.not","strong":"0408","transliteration":